                <note rend="inline" type="source">882.5048/362: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Chargé in Liberia</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Reber</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-11-29T11:00:00-05:00">November 29, 1930—11
                        a.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>107. Your 162, November 22, noon. Department has received request from the
                    Liberian Consul General<anchor n="46" xml:id="d344-f1"/> under instructions from
                    his Government for the Department to transmit the memorandum which the Secretary
                    of State delivered to him November 17. The following is the text of the
                    memorandum:</p>
                <p>[Here follows text of the memorandum, printed on <ref target="#pg369">page
                        369</ref>.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Cotton</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
